Z||000010||M King||12-31-1999||12:12 AM||||I have only seen about 4 fieros in my life.And I love the cars and allways keep a sharp eye out for them when traveling. Once I saw one with my dad in the firebird in Indiana it was tooling around and fishtailing.(I was debating wither or not our 99 firebird was faster then the Fiero) I think it was a rad notchback SE.It probably had to be a six banger to be fishtailing the way it was. It was in very good shape. Another was a purple notchback I think a 2m6 at a old Rolls Royce shop with my grandpa (I sware I was outside the whole time looking at that car).My grandpa though I was nuts not even looking at the expensive cars in the shop. But I think the fiero was/is a better car then any dern rooly:-). I also saw 2 on a trip back from Toronto, a gray and a red 84. And the ONLY fastback I ever have seen was a yellow 88GT with T-Tops (it was in toronto). WOW it was hot. I can't wait to get my fiero in 2 months. I will have about two thousand dollars save up by then, so I will probably look for a 2m6 or something to that nature. I dought I can get a GT with 2K. Anyways im sure youu are all sick of me by now. Bye Bye, and think of yourselfs as VERY lucky to own such cool cars.||||reg||9
Z||000011||Monkeyman||12-31-1999||04:28 AM||||It might be kinda difficult to find a fastback GT in good shape for 2 grand (tho not impossible), but it shouldn't be any problem to find a notchback ('85) GT in good shape for that kind of monkey (er...I mean money).  <P>Bengal4--Yup!  I AM everywhere, just like jolly old St. Nick! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Seriously (well...), I drove a truck for 15 years and covered the country many, many times.  I've been to Canada, Mexico, Alaska, and lower 48 in a truck and to Germany, England, and Scotland in the military.||||reg||1
